course: dictionary
lesson: 7674
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists them as numbered senses, and you choose the one that fits the sentence. «Propose» is a good example: it can mean to suggest an idea, to ask someone to marry you, or to plan to do something.
explain: The context tells you which meaning is right. «I propose we have a picnic» is about a plan for everyone to think about, so it means suggest. If the sentence is about a ring and a question, the context shows it means marriage.
explain: Formal writing often uses propose to mean intend or plan. «What do you propose to do?» is a polite way of asking what someone plans to do. Always check: which meaning makes sense in this sentence?
fact: Propose means to suggest a plan or idea for others to think about.
fact: Propose can also mean to ask someone to marry you.
fact: Propose can mean to intend or plan: «What do you propose to do?»
fact: Propose can also mean to suggest someone for a job or a vote.
fact: «Alfred Wegener proposed in 1912 that continents drift», but most scientists rejected the idea until the 1960s.
exercise: «I propose we have a picnic on Friday.» What does propose mean here? | Ask someone to marry you | Plan to be quiet | Vote someone out of the club | *Suggest a plan for others to think about
exercise: «He proposed to her under the old oak tree, with a ring in his hand.» What does proposed mean here? | *To ask someone to marry you | To leave early | To suggest a picnic | To vote for the best team
exercise: «What do you propose to do about the broken window?» What does propose mean here? | To suggest someone for a job | To shout loudly | *To intend or plan | To ask someone to marry you
test: «Alfred Wegener proposed in 1912 that continents drift.» What does proposed mean here? | To plan a holiday | To give up | *To suggest an idea for others to think about | To ask someone to marry
test: The school council will vote on the idea Mia proposed at the meeting. What does proposed mean here? | To intend to leave | *To suggest an idea for others to think about | To ask someone to marry you | To suggest someone for a job
exam: «Dad proposed that we go swimming.» Which meaning fits best? | Ask Mum to marry him | Give the swimming pool a new name | *Suggest a plan for the family to think about | Plan to stay at home forever
